<title>SINGAPORE: Wassall Asia 1996 net profit up 313 pct.</title>
<headline>Wassall Asia 1996 net profit up 313 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     0.73  vs  0.10</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.80  vs  0.80</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    1.30  vs  0.30</p>
<p>    Turnover				37.72  vs 41.04</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.01  vs  0.03</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.23  vs  0.20</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     0.95  vs  1.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 1.26  vs  0.82</p>
<p>    Tax					0.53  vs  0.72</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil  vs  0.08     (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 2, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: June 12, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Trailer axle-maker Wassall Asia Pacific Ltd is a unit of London-listed Wassall plc. It said good second-half performance helped off-set a first-half fall in activity. Despite economic downturn, its forecast for 1997 was satisfactory. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
